# The index repair fixture is a WiredTiger data directory stored one gzip stream per file. None
# of those streams happens to contain a NUL byte, so git's own binary detection reads them as
# text, and a checkout with `core.autocrlf` would rewrite the CR and LF bytes inside the
# compressed data. Nothing would report that; the repair test would simply fail to unpack a
# directory it could no longer regenerate.
tests/fixtures/** binary
